WEBVTT

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.970
Nine, ten, eleven people.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:15.180
I haven't cooked for that
many people in a long time.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.510
Do you cook often, Kasane?

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:19.220
Hardly at all.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.770
But I hear Yuito does sometimes.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:24.980
The bowls are here,
if I remember correctly.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.940
How'd you know?

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:33.070
All the Sumeragi family's shelters
are the same.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.400
They are?

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.610
Let me help with that.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:37.700
Really?

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.370
I appreciate it.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:45.830
Mother?

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:48.790
To think we could spend time
together like this.

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:31.270
"Wakana's Resolve"

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:39.200
Good morning, Yuito.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.240
Morning.

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:41.990
Feeling okay?

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:44.370
Yeah. I'm...

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:47.040
What about you, Mom?

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:51.000
They say time travel places
a heavy load on the brain.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.840
I'm fine, but thanks for asking.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.510
Kasane has brought me up to speed.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:01.130
That, combined with the data
I received via BABE,

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:04.510
has helped me understand
much of what transpired.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:07.140
I told her about Karen, too.

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:15.730
Psionics sure are also handy
at moments like this.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.780
You're good at that, Yuito.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:22.490
I really like to cook.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.490
I can also do this.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.670
That's amazing.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.500
I'll go do the laundry.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:37.630
Kasane.

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:38.670
It's all right.

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:40.420
I'll be back, Mother.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.840
Okay.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.970
Mom, why don't you sit down
and take it easy?

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:52.890
Thank you, but I'm fine.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.520
You remind me of your father.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:59.110
What? You don't mean that.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:01.360
Kaito looks much more like him.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.820
Everyone says I don't look like Dad.

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:07.370
I don't mean your looks. It's your manner.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:11.450
How is Kaito? Are you two getting along?

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:15.580
He's fine, but I wouldn't
say we get along.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:17.000
I see.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.590
Listen, Yuito...

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:20.960
About your father...

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:25.760
He saved me from being killed by Togetsu.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:28.140
He was a kind and gentle man.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.640
And Kaito said he'd change this nation.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:36.100
Your brother set his sights
on politics from an early age.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.940
Kaito and I...

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.980
Don't worry.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:45.530
You are both our sons, after all.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:51.790
Good morning!

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.000
Thank you for breakfast.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.710
I was wondering...

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:02.050
Why don't you get pulled back
into your time?

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:06.340
Even though it's weak,
I have the power of the Red Strings.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:10.100
But we still must hurry, right?

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:11.390
That's right.

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:15.560
The dimension entanglements within
the Kunad Gate must be eliminated,

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.150
or the world will eventually be destroyed.

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.440
Dimension entanglements?

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:24.150
They're what remains
after interfering with time.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:30.120
The Kunad Gate is a transient dimensional
hole that appears during time travel.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.540
But due to the resonance between
Yuito and Kasane's power,

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:36.920
it persists in a distorted state.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:40.090
Future Yuito said something like that.

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:44.760
Time travel through a distorted gate

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:48.010
results in dimension entanglements.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:53.260
But if we can untangle them,
we can close the Kunad Gate.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:55.640
How do we do that?

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:58.060
Yuito, Kasane.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:02.770
You must enter the Kunad Gate together.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:11.320
Within it is a conceptual space that
exists only for Red Strings users.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:14.330
You mean that place
with all the weird imagery?

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:19.210
That's right. Togetsu calls
it the Chronos Terminal.

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:21.500
The Chronos Terminal.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:26.720
Based on the name, it must be like
a station or juncture for time travel.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:31.510
So then only Yuito and
Kasane can perceive it.

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:35.970
That's why we didn't notice it
when we traveled to the future.

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:38.890
Red Strings users need
not travel through time.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:42.270
Simply coming in contact
with the Chronos Terminal

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:44.360
triggers an entanglement.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:47.110
As for where in time
the entanglements lie,

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:50.110
you must go locate them yourself.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:54.830
So then Yuito and Kasane
really are our only hope.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:58.370
But if they use the Red Strings again...

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:01.000
Yuito, don't put yourself at risk.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:02.170
Got it.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.800
Okay, let's do this.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:23.480
Mother, let's go.

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:26.320
Something wrong?

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:32.070
I'm so happy you grew up
to be such a wonderful person.

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:36.410
I can't take any credit for that,
of course.

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:41.460
I am truly sorry that I abandoned you.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:46.590
You don't have to apologize.
You were almost killed.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:51.590
And I don't remember much
about the time I spent in Togetsu.

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:53.090
Plus...

00:07:55.550 --> 00:08:00.020
...after I came to Suoh, I had Naomi,
the best big sister ever.

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:07.270
Then you'll have to thank her
for that, won't you?

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:08.730
Yeah.

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:16.200
After all that has happened,
she still calls me Mother.

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:19.120
Shall we?

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.330
Okay.

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:30.340
Dimension entanglements should
appear as tangled Red Strings.

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:33.260
You two will know how to untangle them.

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:37.640
Get out of there if things go south.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:41.020
Right. And my mom...

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:43.600
You don't have to worry.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:45.520
We will protect Wakana.

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:46.770
Thanks.

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:48.110
We're grateful.

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:54.400
All right. Are you ready?

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.780
Kasane, you good?

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:58.030
Yes.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:00.580
I want you both to concentrate.

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:03.750
Picture the Chronos Terminal in your mind.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.380
The Chronos Terminal.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.880
We <i>will </i>untangle the Red Strings.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:22.600
Looks like we made it.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:23.890
Yeah.

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:27.270
Yuito. Kasane. This way.

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:28.440
Mother.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:35.700
You can see it, can't you?
The entanglements are just ahead.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.200
Thank you, Mother.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:38.990
We can handle the rest.

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:41.410
All right, but be careful.

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:51.290
There they are.

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:59.590
We must untangle each point in time.

00:09:59.590 --> 00:10:00.930
First off...

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:05.230
That day at the old OSF Hospital.

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:22.620
We've entered the dimension entanglement.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.410
If we use our Red Strings power...

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:26.870
We should be able to untangle it.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:51.650
We can't do this separately.
We must work together.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.570
Come on, focus.

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:54.820
Okay.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:00.110
Some help here!

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:01.410
Got it!

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:13.500
All right.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:14.710
Next.

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:20.630
I think we got this.

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:23.430
You're amazing, Kasane.
Just like a big sis.

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:27.180
What's that supposed to mean?

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:30.390
Well, you <i>were </i>born first, so...

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:32.350
But we're the same age.

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:36.150
Kyoka said you were in cold sleep.

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:39.280
In any case, I'm so grateful.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:40.860
For what?

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:47.290
For saving me that day. Thank you.

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:50.410
I've never properly thanked you.

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:52.960
Why now out of the blue?

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:57.960
Ever since that day,
I've been able to harness my power.

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:02.550
I always felt like you had
shared some of yours with me.

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:05.720
Psionic power can't be shared.

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:08.930
I know that, but...

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:15.690
Because we met that day, I'm alive today,

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:19.280
and I was able to achieve
my goal of joining the OSF.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:21.900
So, I wanted to thank you, Kasane.

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:23.700
You saved me.

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:28.200
You're welcome.

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:29.910
You happy now?

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:32.620
All right, this should wrap it up.

00:12:53.140 --> 00:12:54.190
What's next?

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:56.400
Suoh City 50 years in the future.

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:01.110
The entanglement from
the time I met the future you.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:12.790
This is Suoh 50 years in the future?

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:18.250
Let's go. I know where it is.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:21.090
Hey, wait!

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:27.050
Yuito.

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:30.470
Have you ever thought
about changing history?

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:33.600
You mean by traveling to the past?

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:36.810
Wouldn't that create a new entanglement?

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:40.020
I mean after the Kunad Gate disappears.

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:43.110
What if you could freely travel
back and forth through time?

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:47.700
I've thought about it.

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:51.870
I still regret that I didn't do
something different that day.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:53.450
Yuito.

00:13:54.540 --> 00:14:02.050
If I'm gonna die, I'd at least like to
know what I should've done different.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:05.470
I didn't have an answer for him.

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:11.970
Then don't you want to use the Red Strings
to change the past?

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:14.180
No, I don't.

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:19.230
Even if you change the past,
you don't know what the future holds.

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:25.940
If Nagi hadn't become my friend,
he might not have been caught up in this.

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:31.910
And if I hadn't met Nagi, I wouldn't
have aspired to keep up with him.

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:36.120
I don't think it would be right
to change past events like that.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:40.040
Nagi must've had his own future
he was aiming for.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:43.130
You can't fix the past
if it creates entanglements.

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:44.550
Yeah.

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:48.340
Changing someone's life
to be the way you want it...

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:51.050
...that's just not right.

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:54.970
I'm sorry for asking
such a strange question.

00:14:54.970 --> 00:15:00.190
But I'm surprised to hear
you feel like I do about it.

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:05.780
I probably would've had a different answer
if I'd been asked that years ago.

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:10.110
Maybe the way I see the world changed
a little after I met you and the others.

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:13.030
Yeah, I feel the same way.

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:17.290
We're actually more alike than I thought.

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:20.040
I think it's a bit premature
to assume that.

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:22.460
Right, sorry.

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:30.090
I thought this might be it.

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:38.560
We'll start from the right.

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:40.140
O-Okay.

00:15:54.410 --> 00:15:57.200
Kasane. You all right?

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:59.080
Sorry. I'm fine.

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:10.090
All right, now for the left side.

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:11.010
Okay.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:26.020
Kasane, hang in there! Just a bit more!

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:28.230
I've got this one!

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:30.110
All that's left is that one!

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:46.460
Kasane!

00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:49.340
I'm fine.

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:51.210
One more to go.

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:53.260
Yeah.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.300
Isn't that...?

00:16:57.300 --> 00:16:59.390
The Sumeragi crest.

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:03.350
Oh, yeah! This is what I saw
the first time I came here!

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:05.480
It's just like Mother said.

00:17:05.480 --> 00:17:08.940
Psionics like us need but come
in contact with the Chronos Terminal

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:10.940
to trigger an entanglement.

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:19.280
Karen?!

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:21.750
What just happened?!

00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:23.080
I don't know!

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:25.540
But it doesn't look good!

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:26.460
You ready?!

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:27.670
Yeah!

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:34.380
Of all the times to hit my power limit!

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:36.890
This is not good! Faster!

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:56.700
Did we do it?

00:17:59.370 --> 00:18:02.040
Yuito. Kasane.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:18.970
We made it back.

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:22.390
You're both in one piece. What a relief.

00:18:22.390 --> 00:18:25.430
Yeah, we did it, barely.

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:27.230
The gate should now be...

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:30.810
Why's it still here?

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:37.280
Well done.

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:39.570
You both gave it your all.

00:18:39.570 --> 00:18:40.870
It's okay now.

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:42.330
Yeah, but...

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:47.000
Mother, we unraveled the tangles,
so why is the gate still there?

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:51.500
Leave the rest to me.

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:52.460
What?

00:18:52.460 --> 00:18:53.920
Mother?

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:57.340
You've made so many wonderful friends.

00:18:57.340 --> 00:19:02.510
Those connections are worth more
than any of the Red Strings.

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:04.560
Always cherish them.

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:10.770
Thank you for growing up
so big and strong.

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:13.650
Mom! Are you returning to the past?!

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:17.740
If you return, Togetsu will...!

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:19.950
It must be done.

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:21.570
Forgive me.

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:25.790
But if I stay any longer,
I don't think I could say goodbye.

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:32.540
Wait!

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:34.880
There's still so much
I want to talk about!

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:36.130
Mother!

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:41.840
Yuito. Kasane.

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:46.680
May your future be bright.

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:50.980
Mother.

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:52.350
Mom!

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:15.090
"Warning"

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:19.800
We unraveled the entanglement
from when Mother time traveled, but...

00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:25.600
She told us that the Kunad Gate
would persist as long as she was here.

00:20:25.600 --> 00:20:28.520
She left a message for you guys.

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:32.480
Yuito. Kasane.

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:36.480
Forgive me for leaving like this.

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:40.190
I should've personally
told you what I must do.

00:20:40.190 --> 00:20:44.780
But I didn't think I could
without breaking down.

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:48.240
I'm returning to my own time.

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:51.580
Or should I say, I've already returned.

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:57.840
I've been thinking about all this ever
since I received that data from BABE.

00:20:57.840 --> 00:21:03.380
I must play the part allotted
to me back in my time.

00:21:05.720 --> 00:21:09.810
In order for me to receive
the data sent from Togetsu,

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:15.270
Togetsu must recover my brain
and connect it to BABE.

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:21.280
I know this must be hard for both of you.

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:24.700
But you've made me so happy.

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:30.740
I was able to see my cherished children
become fine young adults.

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:37.170
I may surrender my brain,
but not that glimpse of the future.

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:41.880
Knowing you two, you'll be just fine,
no matter what happens.

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:47.470
Thank you for being born,

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:50.350
and for surviving,

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:52.720
and making me happy.

00:21:56.310 --> 00:22:01.650
Kaito, Yuito, Kasane, Joe...

00:22:01.650 --> 00:22:05.820
"Executing Script..."
"Danger"

00:22:05.990 --> 00:22:06.820
"Memory blackout. Erasure complete."

00:22:12.990 --> 00:22:16.960
I pray that the happiness you gave me

00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:20.790
is returned to you many times over.

00:22:20.790 --> 00:22:23.960
Yuito, Kasane...

00:22:23.960 --> 00:22:25.630
I love you.

00:22:25.630 --> 00:22:27.050
"End of Message"

00:22:34.060 --> 00:22:41.900
<i>I've been a prisoner</i>
<i>of my own longing</i>

00:22:43.690 --> 00:22:51.490
<i>The shimmering heat signals me to halt</i>

00:22:51.490 --> 00:22:53.620
<i>There's a stranger in me</i>

00:22:53.620 --> 00:22:56.120
<i>I'll fly high so I won't be scared</i>

00:22:56.120 --> 00:23:01.380
<i>By this new self I've never seen</i>

00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:03.170
<i>I'm spreading my wings</i>

00:23:03.170 --> 00:23:05.510
<i>Bird in florid flight</i>

00:23:05.510 --> 00:23:10.220
<i>Lift your eyes to the scarlet sky</i>

00:23:10.220 --> 00:23:15.430
<i>Overtaken by the mighty wind</i>

00:23:15.430 --> 00:23:20.600
<i>The view unfolds upon a world</i>
<i>that begins turning</i>

00:23:20.600 --> 00:23:25.070
<i>Amid the intermingling light</i>

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:30.950
<i>I keep searching for tomorrow</i>

00:23:30.950 --> 00:23:32.570
<i>Tomorrow's in your hands</i>

00:23:32.570 --> 00:23:35.790
<i>Don't tell me now you're afraid</i>

00:23:35.790 --> 00:23:37.410
<i>There's no time to waste</i>

00:23:37.410 --> 00:23:40.370
<i>Keep going forward</i>

00:23:40.370 --> 00:23:44.710
<i>There's nothing to be afraid of</i>

00:23:44.710 --> 00:23:46.380
<i>Now, let's go</i>

00:23:46.380 --> 00:23:51.840
<i>Into a brand-new day</i>

00:24:08.320 --> 00:24:11.950
"Brothers"
